# The beads issue export is a DERIVED file: the Dolt DB in .beads/ is the source
# of truth. Every bead rewrites it, so any two concurrent branches conflict here.
#
# Rather than hand-merging two snapshots of a database (the documented beads
# anti-pattern), the `beads-export` driver regenerates the file from the DB.
# The driver lives in .git/config, which git cannot share — run
# `bash scripts/setup-git-merge-driver.sh` (or just `pnpm install`) to install it.
#
# If the driver is not installed, git falls back to a normal conflict and you
# resolve it by hand with: bd export -o .beads/issues.jsonl
.beads/issues.jsonl merge=beads-export

# Generated / vendored files: keep them out of diffs and language stats.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
